    "fullText": "Part 1\nUse the graph to identify the points on the interval\n[a , b]\n[a,b] at which local and absolute extreme values occur.\na\nr\nt\nq\ns\nx\ny\ny = f(x)\nb\nA coordinate system has an unlabeled vertical y-axis and a horizontal x-axis with the following labeled values , listed from left to right: a , q , r , s , t , and b. A curve labeled y = f(x) starts above the x-axis at a and falls from left to right until reaching q , where the curve starts to rise from left to right until reaching r. At r , the curve is below the previous location of the curve at a. Then the curve falls from left to right until reaching s. At s , the curve is below the previous location of the curve at q. After s , the curve rises from left to right until reaching t. At t , the curve is above the previous location of the curve at q and below the previous location of the curve at r. Then the curve starts to fall from left to right , crossing the x-axis , and ends at b. There are vertical dashed lines extending from the labeled values on the x-axis to the curve.\nPart 1\nList the x-values where local minima occur, if any. Select the correct choice and, if necessary, fill in the answer box to complete your choice.\nA.\nThe local minimum value(s) occur(s) at x\n(Use a comma to separate answers as needed.)\nB.\nThere is no local minimum.\nPart 2\nList the x-values where local maxima occur, if any. Select the correct choice and, if necessary, fill in the answer box to complete your choice.\nA.\nThe local maximum value(s) occur(s) at x\n(Use a comma to separate answers as needed.)\nB.\nThere is no local maximum.\nPart 3\nList the x-values where absolute minima occur, if any. Select the correct choice and, if necessary, fill in the answer box to complete your choice.\nA.\nThe absolute minimum value(s) occur(s) at x\n(Use a comma to separate answers as needed.)\nB.\nThere is no absolute minimum.\nPart 4\nList the x-values where absolute maxima occur, if any. Select the correct choice and, if necessary, fill in the answer box to complete your choice.\nA.\nThe absolute maximum value(s) occur(s) at x\n(Use a comma to separate answers as needed.)\nB.\nThere is no absolute maximum.",
